        "original_id": "13dfb403-953e-5f1d-afb6-414cdb85eac8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Peverett, Jimi Hendrix, Charlie Huhn, Bryan Bassett\n- Bands: Foghat, Savoy Brown\n- Albums: Family Joules\n\nFacts:\n- James Marshall \"Jimi\" Hendrix, born Johnny Allen Hendrix, was born on November 27, 1942, and was an American rock guitarist, singer, and songwriter.\n- David Jack Peverett, also known as Lonesome Dave, was born on April 16, 1943, and was an English singer and musician.\n- Dave Peverett was the original lead vocalist and rhythm guitarist of Foghat, and he founded Foghat after his tenure in Savoy Brown.\n- Jimi Hendrix died on September 18, 1970.\n- Dave Peverett died on February 7, 2000.\n- Family Joules was the first Foghat album without founding member Dave Peverett.\n- Family Joules was Foghat's first album to feature singer-guitarist Charlie Huhn and guitarist Bryan Bassett.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
